Every day, all over the world, buckets fall from machines, causing serious injuries and even deaths. As reported by OSHA, this is usually caused by the inadvertent detachment of the bucket from the quick coupling of the excavator.
If a quick coupler without a front lock is used and a wrong connection occurs (the operator does not connect the bucket properly), the bucket may fall off the quick coupler at the beginning of the operation.
how is it? By using a quick connector with a front lock, if a wrong connection occurs, the bucket is fixed by the front lock to prevent it from falling.
