7.1 It is interesting to read:
But now I want to talk only about three. About those that are most often used in the description of the content of aquarium fish.
For example, water hardness. Not only is it of several types, it is also measured in different degrees, depending on the country.
Why these parameters "Non-living"?
These are parameters that are not influenced by the inhabitants of the aquarium, such as fish, plants or bacteria. Rather, it is these parameters that affect them more.
Read necessarily! They are very important for the health of your fish.
Temperature is not a simple, but the most familiar parameter to us. We meet with her everywhere and feel her every second, although we cannot see her.
Temperature is a very important parameter of water when keeping and breeding fish. Fish are cold-blooded creatures, and they cannot warm us from the inside, so they are completely dependent on the temperature of their environment.
A fast change in it at 4 ° C or more, can lead to a temperature shock and even their death. Therefore, always equalize the temperature at the transplantation of fish after buying or changing the water in the aquarium!
Since the heater can be attributed to important devices in the aquarium, read reviews and buy proven manufacturers. Otherwise, in the event of a breakdown of a substandard device, there is a risk of boiling your fish alive.
A constant hardness is the hardness that does not change during the process of boiling water.
Water hardness must be considered when choosing fish and plants. And it is especially important to take it into account when they are compatible.
And the fish living in the lakesAfrica, conversely adapted to hard water. That's why, for example, it is not recommended to keep cichlids from South America and Africa in the same tank.
Next, I'll tell you how you can influence the hardness of the water in the aquarium. For ease of understanding, I will not distinguish between temporary and permanent stiffness.
Of the quite affordable ways, you can try adding boiled (no sediment) or melted (frozen) water to the aquarium. It is necessary to freeze according to a special scheme, only one third.
How to increase the pH in the aquarium?
Of all the available methods, this is the addition of all the same baking soda.
In water conditioners for changing the composition of water is quite a strong "chemistry", so, use them with extreme caution and always read the instructions!
But if you want to lower and keep the pH level naturally under control, use driftwood in your aquarium. Or add almond leaves there (Catappa).
