(At one of the forums, someone called this frog a “meditating scuba diver.” So, this name describes the frog's behavior with 100% accuracy. And if you get yourself these cute creatures, you can be sure!
Dwarf frog (Hymenochirus boettgeri) - comes from equatorial countries Africa: Zaire, Congo, Cameroon and Nigeria. It prefers to settle in shallow warm silted reservoirs and slowly flowing rivers.
The dwarf frog is not a capricious creature and even the beginning aquarist can create ideal conditions for it. Almost any standard conditions found in aquariums will do.
Aeration is not necessary, but it is necessary to ensure that frogs have access to the open surface of the water for breathing.
It is necessary to ensure that the frogs get their food, because, because of their slowness, they can compete with fish.
Dwarf frog (Hymenochirus boettgeri) Is an omnivorous creature and feeding it is quite simple. There will be everything from shrimp feed (on video), pills for catfish, bloodworms, sliced mussels and shrimp, and ending with dead Mexican cancer (on video).
All its participants are considered to be quite peaceful guys and lived for a long time quite amicably. But nature is nature, and there's nothing to be done.
In general, in one of the fights, the Mexican crayfish lost. Found him without a claw, a pair of legs, but still alive.
But the frogs were very interested in the body of the crayfish, the camera was next to it, and it turned out a good video from the life of the underwater micro world!
