The air from the compressor is fed to the bottom of the filter, where it makes a turn, and with the help of natural forces begins to move to the surface. This creates a reverse thrust, which sucks water through a sponge, and with it everything else.
Airlift filter of a new generation! That is, it turns out that the role of a pump in such a filter is performed by an air compressor, which is located outside, and thus saves the useful space inside the aquarium.
Due to the fact that such a filter does not have any holes, but only a sponge, this filtration option is simply irreplaceable in aquariums with fry and shrimp. Wherever there is a risk of sucking in and ruining someone small and invisible.
So, the new generation filter is a plastic container, where different filtration materials are placed in layers. In my case, the filter also has an angular shape, which is very convenient and saves useful space.
The filter itself is almost silent (only the sound of air bubbles rising to the surface).
Since there is no internal pump, therefore such a filter takes up less space.
