2 Vitamins. Basic types and their characteristics.
5 Vitamins Mode of application.
First is the composition. And if this is not a special food, then the composition in the product will be very incomplete.
In the frozen feed there are none at all. And if you constantly feed fish, for example, frozen bloodworms, then without additional additives they will have a permanent vitamin deficiency.
And, vitamins very help to reduce the acclimatization time after buying and moving fish to a new aquarium. And during the treatment they will not be superfluous.
Vitamin C - enhances immunity, disease resistance and strengthens the skeleton.
There are two main types of vitamin preparations for fish, and they are divided according to the method of application. The first type is a concentrate and is used as an additive in feed and water.
Sera Fishtamin - food additive in the form of an emulsion, produced on the basis of concentrates of various vitamins. It is mainly used during feeding, but can be used and dissolved in aquarium water.
To maintain useful properties, do this in the evening, after turning off the light in the aquarium. Otherwise, vitamins will disintegrate and there will be no effect.
If you additionally do not use vitamin supplements, then a disease with the name Avitaminosis may occur in the fish.
