3.2 Ammonia in the aquarium!
Pistia is a malicious weed and pest in the wild!
And all because Pistia it grows incredibly quickly and over time can completely subjugate the entire reservoir. Pisty in nature.
Also, there are some types of mosquitoes, such asMansonia,who use pistia for its reproduction. And consequently, the more a plant captures a pond, the more mosquitoes in its district will become.
This is why the plant Pistia (Pistia stratiotes) is an invasive and is subject to stringent measures of extermination, in most countries.
Due to very rapid growth and unpretentiousness, Pistia can be used as an indispensable assistant in maintaining the chemical balance in the aquarium, and because the plant does not need soil, it is very convenient to use in aquariums with fry. The plant will absorb very badly ammonia и nitrites ,and will not poison young fish.
Also, in the roots floating and hanging like fairy tentacles, the so-called “living dust” loves to wind up. Microorganisms that serve as excellent food for fry in the first days of life.
