Test temperature: The test temperature is +70℃, and the tolerance range is ±2℃.
Test methods: The sample table was placed in a high temperature test box, heated to +70℃ at a rate not greater than 1℃/min, maintained for 72 hours after stabilization, and then cooled to the reference temperature at a rate not greater than 1℃/min. Then, the appearance of the meter was checked and the basic error was tested.
Test methods: The electricity meters under test were placed in a low-temperature test chamber. According to the indoor/outdoor type of the electricity meters, they were cooled to -25℃ or -40℃ at a rate not greater than 1℃/min.
Then, the appearance of the electricity meter was checked and the insulation strength test and basic error test were carried out. The test results show that the insulation of the electric energy meter should not be broken down (the pulse voltage is 0.8 times of the specified amplitude), and the electric energy meter has no damage or information change and can work correctly.
