The remote smartt electricity meter of Linyang takes the real-time sampling of the user’s power supply voltage and current, and then integrates the circuit of the electricity meter to convert it into a proportional pulse output, which is processed and controlled by the single chip microcomputer to display the pulse as the electricity consumption and output to realize the electric energy measurement.
2. The event recording function of remote smart electricity meter can help utility check power theft at any time.
The integrated smart meter has built-in anti-reversing device and monitoring function, which can measure the operating parameters such as voltage, current (including zero line), active power and power factor, and the reversal of the meter will not exceed one turn. In addition, if the meter has abnormal circuit such as voltage phase failure, voltage loss, current loss, power loss, super power and malignant load, the meter will send an alarm signal to customers and trip automatically.
All electricity data could be remotely real-time monitored and dimensional analyzed. If you have found abnormal event, the system will immediately send a warning notice through computers, cell phones, text messaging and other ways and automatic trip the meter.
