This tool is what measures the overall performance of your channel. You need to master it if you want to grow your channel efficiently and gain subscribers on Youtube.
Once you have entered the Channel dashboard, select Analytics from the left-hand side bar. From here, you will see five analytics tabs: Overview, Reach, Engagement, Audience, and Revenue.
However, there is one particular section that requires your attention to determine the best time to upload to Youtube, and that is the report on ‘When your viewers are on YouTube’. You can see it right under the main audience chart, and be ready for the next step.
Step 3: Identify the golden days and hours of your Youtube channel
You will be presented with a purple bar chart. It displays the days and times most of your viewers are on Youtube.
To put it simply, just ask yourself whether you would upload your video when everybody is asleep or at work. No one would be there to watch your new content right?
Now when you look at this chart, you will see the hour and the day. But what about these purple bars with different shades?
Firstly, there is one thing you need to remember: the darker the purple shade, the more of your viewers are online. So the tactic here is to count the days with the highest number of darkest purple boxes.
Finally, it’s the matter of narrowing out the best hours of the best days, which as we have mentioned above, are the bars with the darkest purple shade.
As a general rule, it takes quite some time for Youtube to analyze and index your video. Therefore, don’t wait until the exact prime time to upload your video.
Instead, you can upload your video two hours before the golden hours. This allows your video to have enough to be processed and categorized by Youtube (especially if yours is a high definition video).
Combine with the views you will get from the prime time and voila!
Another way, however, is to upload your video privately, then publish it when the right time comes. The reasons are the same as before, and you get more time to write a good title, fill in relevant details in your description, and upload a good thumbnail.
