The anticorrosion process of electric prefabricated cabin includes sand blasting, hot spraying zinc and paint spraying. Each process contains many methods and requirements, which need to pass strict requirements and anticorrosion testing.
Sand is the first step on the prefabricated tank anti-corrosion treatment, the purpose is to remove impurities on the surface of the hull, convenient and subsequent work, with the purpose of 20 corundum as material, to burnish of hull, jet cleaning level to steel surface Sa21/2, after the completion of the surface of the steel or has a certain roughness, this is normal phenomenon,
We all know that the most simple and effective way to do anti-corrosion treatment is to spray paint, but in order to ensure better anti-corrosion effect, there is another process before painting, that is hot spray zinc.
The method of use is to put two zinc wires on the spraying machine, turn on the power to produce an arc, melt the zinc wires, and spray them to the prefabricated cabin under the action of compressed air.
