With the popularity of photovoltaic energy, more and more places to use the photovoltaic grid-connected cabinet, but the general population lack of professional knowledge of electricity, when the photovoltaic grid-connected cabinet tripping do not know what is the cause, the following article to explain it in detail!
Therefore, when the photovoltaic grid-connected cabinet switches trip, the reason is that the switch may appear overcurrent, overvoltage, overtemperature, leakage current. The following analysis of the causes of each case of the solution.
This fault is the most common, circuit breaker selection is too small or the quality is not up to standard.When designing, the maximum current of the circuit should be calculated first. The rated current of the switch should exceed 1.1 to 1.2 times the maximum current of the circuit.Judgment basis: it is not tripped at ordinary times, but only when the weather is good and the power of the photovoltaic system is large.
Generally, the single pole is 250V. If this voltage is exceeded, it may trip.There may be two reasons: one is the wrong selection of the rated voltage type of the circuit;Second, when the power of the photovoltaic system is greater than the power of the load, the inverter increases the voltage to send electricity out.
Solution: Replace circuit breakers with higher rated voltage, or cables with larger wire diameters, and reduce line impedance.
Solution: rewire, or replace the circuit breaker.
Line or other electrical failure, leakage of other electrical equipment, leakage of line, damage of components or insulation layer of DC line.
Solution: Test and replace faulty equipment and wires.
