The function, function and principle of anti-islanding-device of photovoltaic power station
Let’s start by explaining what islanders are:
When the power is lost on the grid side, maintenance personnel need to repair it. At this time, the photovoltaic side is still in the normal power generation state, and the anti-islanding protection device will issue a command to the grid-connected switch to make it trip, so as to well ensure the life safety of maintenance personnel on both sides of the photovoltaic.
When the frequency, voltage or overload operation occurs on the photovoltaic side or any side of the grid side, the anti-islanding protection device will also quickly issue a command to the grid-connected switch to make it trip, so as to well ensure that the main equipment on both sides is not hurt and avoid the further expansion of the accident.
When the fault is removed, both sides of the photovoltaic are in a normal state.At this time, the anti-islanding protection device will detect the relevant signals, and automatically close the grid-connection switch, so that it can work normally, eliminating the cumbersome manual grid-connection.With loss of pressure tripping, pressure detection of automatic closing functions and so on.
