This method is the use of electrode reaction to form a coating in the workpiece surface. The main methods are:
In the electrolyte solution, the workpiece is the cathode, which can form a coating film on the surface under the action of external current, which called electroplating.
In the electrolyte solution, the workpiece is the anode, which can form a anodized layer on the surface under the action of external current, which called anodizing, such as aluminum alloy anodizing.
Because interaction between chemical substances of solution and workpiece without external current which can form coating film on the workpiece surface, which called chemical conversion film. Such as bluing, phosphating, passivating, chromium salt treatment and so on.
This method is making the material melting or thermal diffusion in the high temperature conditions to form coating film on the surface of the workpiece. The mainly methods are:
Put metal parts into the molten metal to form the coating film on the surface of the workpiece, which called hot-dip plating, such as hot-dip galvanizing, hot aluminum and so on.
