Gerber file mainly describes the collection of document format of PCB image (line layer, solder resistance layer, character layer, etc.) drilling and milling data, which needs to be provided to PCBA processing plant when PCBA quotation is made.
SMT is the abbreviation of “Surface Mounted Technology”, which refers to the process of solder paste printing, sheet components mounting and reflow ovensoldering on PCB board. 6.
Reflow soldering is to put the pasted PCB into the reflow solder machine, and through the high temperature inside, the paste solder paste will be heated into liquid, and finally the welding will be completed by cooling and solidification.
QFP is short for “Quad Flat Pack”, which refers to a surface-assembled integrated circuit in a thin plastic package with short airfoil leads on four sides.
SMT N ozzle replacement time: because there are various components on the printed circuit board, need different nozzle, SMT nozzle on the installation head often can not suck away all types of components, so the general SMT design has the function of automatic replacement of nozzle.
worktable movement time: refers to the time of X, Y table to drive the printed circuit board from the original position to the current installation position. For platform machines, it refers to the time of the cantilever XY drive shaft to drive the placement head from the previous position to the current placement position.
