In this simple process, the substrate is immersed in a coating bath, which usually has a low viscosity, so that the coating can return to the bath when the substrate appears. This method is often used on porous substrates.
In the curtain coating process, a bath with grooves on the base allows the continuous curtain of coating to fall into the gap between the two conveyors. The object to be coated, such as a door, passes along the conveyor at a controlled speed, thus receiving the coating on its upper surface.
