Surely you have wondered how to upload photos to instagram from your computer, then keep reading ...
If this is your case, you have probably resorted to the tedious procedure of sending the photos to your email and downloading them to your mobile or maybe you have connected your USB cable to your computer to download them to the phone and from there to Instagram. Because this option is not available in the web version.
Well, with this in mind I want to share the way to know how to upload photos to Instagram from the PC, or those that you have done with your camera and not with the Smartphone. Without so much protocol.
Yes, just as you can download simulators that turn your computer into the video game console you want, it is also possible to download applications to simulate that your computer is an Android mobile and I'm going to tell you what they are.
Then you must download the Blue Stacks app and install it on your computer. Once the installation is done you can search and download Instagram
Create a folder for the photos that you will upload to Instagram. Access the application and you can use it as if you were doing it from your mobile, you could even use the web cam to make your selfies.
Gramblr offers you the possibility of edit your photos, check your history and even program Your publications
Some users have reported that with Gramblr they have had problems to place hashtags to your photos so it's something you should consider before using it.
Other options to upload photo to instagram from computer
This “official” application allows you to review your posts, give likes, make comments, search and send messages, such as the desktop version we knew so far.
If you have Windows 10 on your computer, just click on the camera icon in the upper left corner of your screen and your webcam will be activated. It works best if your monitor or screen is touch.
You can easily access it from your computer, without downloading any application, or updating your version of Windows. This way you can upload photos to instagram from the PC, but there are some inconveniences.
You will not be able to edit the photos, or apply our Instagram filters, if we can adjust the format and rotate the photo. Nor can we upload videos.
For the videos we may have to wait a little longer. But how do you do it?
Go to your profile Instagram from your computer
A menu will be displayed to the right of your profile, you must select the second option from left to right “Toggle device toolbar” or in Spanish “Change the device toolbar”
It works the same way, by clicking on the icon of the camera to the center of the lower toolbar, it will take you to your image files from where you will select the one you want to publish. You must have already edited it if you want to improve its appearance
The next step is to click on the upper right corner where it says "NEXT"
Click in the upper right corner “SHARE"And voila, in principle you will not see the update in the Web version, but if you enter from your mobile: There it will be.
With this method you can upload photos to instagram from pc without programs, simply using this web tool.
