Choosing the ideal photos and videos (with adequate aesthetics, sharpness and above all that are relevant to the community that you have created on Instagram) is not a simple task, but without doubt another factor that could take a long time is the most auspicious days and hours. to publish and program on instagram so that your content appears in the feed of your followers.
In today's post I bring you the best tools to schedule Instagram posts (video and photo):
Application formerly known by name Latergramme, is a tool that integrates the use of mobile and PC to program and publish content on your Instagram account, although it also allows you to program for Facebook, Twitter and Pinterest.
You must first enter the later page and register with your email or your Instagram account (preferably) once registered, log in:
In calendar, we can upload and schedule publications with date and time and display them to the right of the screen on a calendar, worth the redundancy, with a view of the week or month.
To schedule a post, you must select photo What do you want to post, click on the “create post” button, you write the caption with the #hashtags and mentions you want, then set the date and time in which you would like to publish and finally press "save" and your post will be scheduled and you can view it in the calendar.
In the Media library You can view all the images you have uploaded to Later, filter them by "used" and "unused" to better handle the content you have pending.
In general the free version is quite useful, however it has the limitation of only allow you to schedule 30 publications per month And from a single account, although this for personal users may suffice, if you are very active on Instagram and have more content, you can go for any of the paid versions that Later offers.
While it may be more convenient to plan posts from the PC, Later's mobile app allows us to schedule and publish from our mobile regardless of the computer.
Enter the app from your mobile, log in with the email and password you used to sign up for the Web version of Later.
Once the image is loaded (this process may take a while depending on the weight of the image), touch it and when it appears in large size click on “Schedule Publication"
The app will ask you when you want to publish, press “Schedule Now"If you don't want to wait to hang your image or"Choose a Time”To schedule it for another time, if you do the latter, you must set the date and time of the publication Publish
Press "Post Now”Will ask you to confirm the Instagram account where you are going to publish, will load the photo and automatically copy the photo caption you had already saved to the clipboard
To use onlypult, you must register and configure your time zone and confirm an email, with the account already confirmed you can synchronize with 1 or more Instagram accounts that must meet some requirements such as being public profiles, being confirmed with an email and telephone number, having more than 5 publications in the account, etc.
To schedule publications go to the tab "Publishing" there, you will see the images and videos posted on your account, and you can schedule upload individual posts (a single photo or video), a gallery (several photos in a single post) or even upload bulk 20 individual posts.
