The Instagram algorithm starts working in the 2016 year and since then users complain about the visibility of their posts. According to its developers, its function was to prioritize the content visible in the feed from preferences of each user.
6 Other factors that condition the operation of the Instagram algorithm
7.2 Evaluate the hashtags you use
7.6 Variety in the contents
This algorithm is based on engagement and determines the content priority that you can see when accessing the Start menu on Instagram based on your activity within the application and this includes:
I like them or likes
Searches you have done
Other variables that determine what you can see when you browse Instagram are:
Impressions or number of times the contents are viewed
This second algorithm establishes the preeminence of some contents over others when you search for a hashtag. time based in which the audience reacts to the publication.
Experiments conducted by Spanish social media students in Mallorca allowed them to determine that this algorithm prioritize the images that impact to many users in a short time.
With the appropriate number of interactions in a certain time it is possible to position in the search of several hashtags one or several photos of the same account, even if it does not have thousands of followers.
The stories of the users whose content you have given I like
Users to the ones you have searched
Number of times you watch each story
It depends on the number of publications and is positioned by the number of interactions. The comments They are the ones that have more weight for this positioning.
Other factors that condition the operation of the Instagram algorithm
The Instagram algorithm study your behavior and presents the most important content for you according to your interaction with what you see. The time you spend looking at a post.
I have tried to publish using five and eleven hashtags and the result in visualizations and impressions has been practically the same. Another test I did was place hashtags as comment in photos previously published and did not favor the visibility of the post.
The first hours in the morning, mid afternoon and at nightfall These are the hours that work best for me, but each account is a world and its audience. Study the behavior of your followers and publish accordingly.
In addition to this: Determine what your best contents are
Evaluate the publications that have worked best with your audience so you can offer similar content. Compare what you share with the trends and what your followers like.
Research hashtags that other users use with interests and content similar to yours and copy those that seem relevant and that may work for you. The niche or market hashtags that relate to your account.
Emoji Hashtags they are another option to consider considering that the younger audience and the Millenials they use them and that will make it easier for you connect with them. Follow the trends and use these hashtags in your posts whenever they are relevant.
El video is privileged content by the Instagram algorithm because it keeps users more time within the application. Especially now that the available live broadcasts y IGTV and the possibility of sharing contents of more than one minute.
The photos alone or in carousel are at the top of searches And it makes sense if we consider that they were originally the reason for being from Instagram, so despite the fluctuations of the algorithm they are my favorite content.
However, he insists and ask for your opinion. Comments are the interaction that most positions on Instagram.
Order tag someone in some publication and leave a comment is another call to action widely used, it is not my favorite because I consider it a bit invasive and can bother people who take care of the privacy of their information, but it can work very well to generate interactions in your post
El use of emojis It is another alternative to humanize your personal or business brand and also helps provide an emotional context to your texts.
There is an unofficial “magic” formula that establishes a certain proportion of content to maintain a feed that is interesting for those who follow you:
% Of 20 promotional content. Information about discounts and special offers.
Take care of the quality of what you publish and add value for other users to connect with your post and so generate engagement.
